  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scaling Up Access to Family Planning Services in Zambia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To improve access to family planning to reduce maternal mortality and enable women and girls to have choice and control over their sexual and reproductive health.  To support over 400,000 women to access contraception for the first time.  The programme emphasises working within the Government of Zambia system in provinces where unmet need is particularly high to ensure sustainability of results and embed improvements within existing systems.</narrative>
  </description>
